+++ b/docs/architecture.md
@@ -302,13 +302,21 @@ Both adapters keep a local render snapshot, apply `WorkLeafEvent` values to that
 `TerminalUi`, and render from the cache rather than fetching a full controller snapshot for every
 frame. They own terminal event-loop concerns such as insert mode, prompt mode, `Ctrl-W` navigation,
 SGR mouse clicks, SGR mouse wheel scrolling of the right pane, chunked terminal input parsing,
-rendering invalidation, and polling background workers. Insert mode sends chat text to the selected
-agent session, or to `command-agent` when the Work Leaf command surface is selected. Bracketed-paste
-newlines and Shift+Enter are chat prompt line breaks. A plain Enter submits the buffered chat text.
+visual-mode copy handling, rendering invalidation, and polling background workers. Insert mode sends
+chat text to the selected agent session, or to `command-agent` when the Work Leaf command surface is
+selected. Bracketed-paste newlines and Shift+Enter are chat prompt line breaks. A plain Enter
+submits the buffered chat text.
 When an agent chat is selected in command mode, `/` focuses the chat, seeds the chat buffer with
 `/`, and enters insert mode so `/status`-style input submits through the same selected-agent chat
 path.
 
+Terminal visual selection is pane-scoped. In command mode, `v` starts character-wise selection,
+`V` starts line-wise selection, and `Ctrl-V` starts block selection in the focused left or right
+pane. Movement keys extend the selection. `y` copies using the active visual kind, and `Y` copies
+the selected rows line-wise. `TerminalUi` computes the selected text from rendered pane lines and
+returns it through `UiAction::CopySelection`; `TerminalApp` records that text, emits an OSC 52
+clipboard sequence on the next frame, and writes a short transcript confirmation.
+
 Clean-review completion prompts are represented as transcript lines rather than as separate session
 DTO fields. `TerminalApp` and `RemoteTerminalApp` detect `FEATURE_DONE_PROMPT`, set the terminal
 completion prompt state in `TerminalUi`, show hidden chats that receive the prompt, and route `yes`
